  pm-pim7,related,"2026-11-16T23:30:31.511Z","harness:claude-code","cli:create:dep",detected
  pm-m0fh,related,"2026-11-16T23:30:54.676Z","harness:claude-code","cli:update:dep",detected
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-17T08:37:30.937Z","harness:claude-code","Design (branch fix/secret-guard-reference-literals-and-property-names). scanMutationSecrets now reads each object's own entries once per scan into PayloadEntry rows (name, value, path segment, name matches) shared by the leaf pass and the member pass. Every property name is judged by every rule as its own leaf (token formats, private-context rules and the key-named rules alike), memoized per distinct name per scan. A flagged name's path segment becomes the positional placeholder [key n], its index among the object's own entries, and that segment is used for the name's own finding and for every finding under it in both passes, so paths stay stable and never repeat the name. A name finding carries the new optional SecretGuardFinding field property_name: true; the dedupe key includes it, so a name and its value matching the same rule at the same path are both reported. Array indices stay positions and are never judged as names. CLI warnings still print only rule ids."
  "2026-11-17T09:05:13.968Z","harness:claude-code","Correction to the close actual_result: the 20,000-row repeated-name scan was not measured when that text was written. Measured afterwards on this host with the built SDK, scanMutationSecrets over 20,000 objects that share one credential-shaped property name returned 20,000 findings in 1,240 ms; the spec bounds it at 5,000 ms. The name itself is judged once per scan; the remaining cost is the per-object leaf scan that existed before."
